    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive engine is firing on all cylinders with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (71.91) and **James Wood** (71.49) anchoring the lineup. **Vinnie Pasquantino** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to his dynamic platoon advantage against Bibee, while **James Wood** continues to provide elite daily upside, boosted by a premier leadoff spot and an impressive 0.404 xwOBA. **Corbin Carroll** (70.70) remains a core start despite the slight drag of facing a pitcher with a high SB-hold rate; his pure speed profile is non-negotiable for our pursuit of the stolen base category. **Josh Naylor** (70.49) also clocks in as a strong play, largely driven by a favorable matchup against a vulnerable arm in R. Johnson.\n\nThe most challenging decision today was leaving **Austin Riley** (53.62) on the bench. While his pedigree is high, his projected efficiency fell just short of our starters. We opted for the platoon-heavy upside of **Mickey Moniak** (66.00) and the steady production of **Gabriel Moreno** (61.57), as **Austin Riley** lacked the specific situational boosters\u2014park factors and platoon splits\u2014that pushed our lower-order bats into the green. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** (61.66) faces a minor efficiency penalty due to his opponent's ability to control the running game, yet his high placement in the order secures his spot. We are monitoring all lineups closely for late changes, but as it stands, our focus remains on maximizing volume against the weaker arms of the day.",
